%U A398636 148690620215962737662588657018833676562641693874046285450465561804800000000000000
%N A398636 Number of construction sequences of the complete 3-uniform hypergraph on n labeled vertices.
%C A398636 Here a construction sequence means a linear ordering of all vertices and hyperedges in which each hyperedge occurs after its three incident vertices. Equivalently, a(n) is the number of linear extensions of the vertex-hyperedge incidence poset of the complete 3-uniform hypergraph.
%H A398636 P. C. Kainen, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.13186">Construction numbers: How to build a graph?</a>, arXiv:2302.13186 [math.CO], 2023-2024.
%H A398636 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ConstructionNumber.html">Construction Number</a>.
%F A398636 a(n) = (n+m)!*n!/Product_{k=1..n} (k+m-binomial(n-k,r)) where m = binomial(n,r) with r=3.
%e A398636 For n=3, the unique hyperedge must follow all three vertices, so a(3) = 3! = 6.
%t A398636 a[n_] := With[{m=Binomial[n,3]}, Factorial[n+m]*Factorial[n]/Product[k+m-Binomial[n-k,3], {k,1,n}]]
%o A398636 (PARI) a(n) = my(m=binomial(n,3)); (n+m)!*n!/prod(k=1, n, (k+m-binomial(n-k,3))); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Aug 13 2026
